{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data quality data quality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","fileName":"Data Quality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Quality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Big Data Governance and Quality]] · [[Cluster Data Quality and Interpretation]] · [[Evidence-Based Data Decisions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Governance and Quality","Cluster Data Quality and Interpretation","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data quality data quality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","fileName":"Data Quality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Quality","heading":"Data Quality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Data quality is the fitness of data for the decision or analysis it supports. Accuracy, relevance, completeness, consistency, timeliness, and adequate context determine whether a large collection can produce useful conclusions.\n\nVolume does not compensate for poor quality. Errors and irrelevant observations can be amplified by aggregation, while uncertain provenance makes it difficult to explain or correct an outcome.\n\nFor cluster analysis, quality is inseparable from representation. Unrelated features distort proximity, incompatible data types can invalidate a method, and stale domains or unenforced business rules can corrupt results. The source emphasizes accuracy, reliability, timeliness, relevance, and completeness as complementary dimensions maintained through ongoing cleansing.\n\nFor evidence-based decisions, quality also connects the processing pipeline to the decision context. Veracity, provenance, and adequate cleaning determine whether a pattern can be treated as credible evidence rather than merely as a computable result.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Governance and Quality","Cluster Data Quality and Interpretation","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data quality data quality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Quality.md","fileName":"Data Quality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Quality","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n\n[[clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf]]\n\n[[frontiersofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Big Data Governance and Quality","Cluster Data Quality and Interpretation","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}